<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Schloss Burg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">12th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Burg Castle</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Schloss Burg is a castle above the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wupper">Wupper river</a> within the city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/solingen">Solingen</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-rhine-westphalia">North Rhine-Westphalia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. Built in the 12th century by the counts of Berg, it was their main seat until the court moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dusseldorf">Düsseldorf</a> in the late 14th century. It fell into ruin after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-tyrants">the Thirty</a> Years' War and was rebuilt from 1890, and is now a museum of the Bergisches Land.</p></div>
